16#post73516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right, cause in god machine and b&amp;s they changed the exp cost for things ja?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so. I can't remember if there was a particular rule of thumb for which way to round the end result, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T20:09:00-08:00","id":73519,"title":"","content":"Yes. The GMC/B&amp;S/DtD/etc. XP systems changed the costs. Everything is a flat cost and generally much cheaper for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T20:09:13-08:00","id":73520,"title":"","content":"man looking at the gmc updates... good god this is more of a reboot and less about a second edition rules wise right? But the core lore is still the same yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T20:46:28-08:00","id":73529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/73088-ok-so-beats?p=73520#post73520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">man looking at the gmc updates... good god this is more of a reboot and less about a second edition rules wise right? But the core lore is still the same yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. A good comparison would actually be AD&amp;D to AD&amp;D 2nd Edition. They wanted to update the rules, but didn't want to totally invalidate the old system, so they wrote updates that use the same rules framework but clean up a lot of the extraneous subsystems and improve on existing rules technology. It's close enough that you can convert just about anything from before the update without much difficulty, but different enough that you can't really run the material side-by-side without doing some level of conversion work. As far as lore goes... It's basically the same, with a few differences. The lore of the God-Machine and Demon the Descent is all new, but drawn from the existing fiction, and doesn't invalidate any of the previous lore. Blood &amp; Smoke, on the other hand does change a few details from vanilla Requiem's lore. Not so much that it's unrecognizable though. In fact, it's similar enough you kind of have to be looking for the differences to really notice them in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T06:10:15-08:00","id":73681,"title":"","content":"The thing with beats is that besides getting them from resolving any condition (or even getting multiple beats off one) is that, considering Aspirations? you literally get XP from deciding and eventually enhacting the way the stories turn.<br /> <br /> Short term aspirations are the holy cow of Beats: you're getting mugged couple of sample aspirations - escape with your wallet; not get stabbed at any cost; make sure the criminal ends up in jail... the list goes on. And this is for a mundane occurance. Add say, the kinds of mysteries you could experience in WoD and the sky is the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T09:38:17-08:00","id":73756,"title":"","content":"You know I hadn't thought about that. I'm sure my player currently abusing Mike Barringer from the demo is gonna looooove that. He stole the suv the glass spirit claimed were driving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:25:37-07:00","id":88631,"title":"","content":"It can take a bit of work switching your group to using Beats, mostly because it's a mindset change. But once both you and your players (or vice versa) get a hand on them, they tend to flow pretty fast. I personally use group beats because I have a fairly large group and some tend to be more outgoing, more into RP, etc than others so if I didn't do group beats the group would be all over the board in terms of power scale.<br /> <br /> The players typically get enough beats for 1-2 xp per session from conditions, dramatic failures, aspirations, damage, etc. I also tend to hand out beats here or there for good RP, cool ideas, and a variety of other things. I also sometimes give a bonus experience point or two at the end of a story if my players handled things or RP'd particularly well. That tends to be enough experience that my group can buy something new or upgrade something on their sheet at the end of each story, at least with starter or low-bonus-xp characters.<br /> <br /> Beats are one of the reasons I love the GMC/B&amp;S updates, the new rules and revisions really help drive players to make and play better characters while making the ST's job that much easier.<br /> <br /> Edit: Spelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 03-11-2014, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}